{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":10000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahsa_Amini_protests"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahsa_Amini_protests:\n| Mahsa Amini protests | |\n| --- | --- |\n| Part of the [Iranian protests against compulsory hijab](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_protests_against_compulsory_hijab \"Iranian protests against compulsory hijab\"), the aftermath of the [death of Mahsa Amini](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_of_Mahsa_Amini \"Death of Mahsa Amini\") and [Gen Z protests in Asia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gen_Z_protests_in_Asia \"Gen Z protests in Asia\") | |\n| Protestors at [Amirkabir University of Technology](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amirkabir_University_of_Technology \"Amirkabir University of Technology\") *(top)* and on [Keshavarz Boulevard](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Keshavarz_Boulevard \"Keshavarz Boulevard\") *(bottom)* | |\n| Date | 16 September 2022 – 2023 |\n| Location | Iran, with solidarity rallies worldwide[[1]](#cite_note-1) |\n| Caused by | [Death of Mahsa Amini](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_of_Mahsa_Amini \"Death of Mahsa Amini\")[[2]](#cite_note-atlantic_whole_generation_revolts-2) |\n| Goals | Revolution,[[3]](#cite_note-3) [civil, political](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_and_political_rights \"Civil and political rights\"), and [women's rights](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Women's_rights \"Women's rights\") reform,[[4]](#cite_note-nbc_iran_warns_the_West-4) other reforms such as the dissolution of the [Guidance Patrol](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guidance_Patrol \"Guidance Patrol\"),[[5]](#cite_note-cbc_st._john's_rally-5) and justice for Mahsa Amini's death |\n| Methods | [Demonstrations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political_demonstration \"Political demonstration\"), [strikes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strike_action \"Strike action\"), [civil disobedience](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_disobedience \"Civil disobedience\"), [civil resistance](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_resistance \"Civil resistance\"), [riots](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riot \"Riot\") |\n| Result | Protest failure: hundreds of people killed and tens of thousands beaten and/or detained in government crackdown |\n| Parties | |\n| |  |  | | --- | --- | | Iranian protesters supported by most of the [Iranian opposition](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_opposition \"Iranian opposition\") organizations and [monarchists](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monarchism_in_Iran \"Monarchism in Iran\") | * [Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") [Government of Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Iran \"Government of Iran\")   + [Police Command](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Police_Command_of_the_Islamic_Republic_of_Iran \"Police Command of the Islamic Republic of Iran\")     - [Guidance Patrol](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guidance_Patrol \"Guidance Patrol\")   + [Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamic_Revolutionary_Guard_Corps \"Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps\")     - [Basij](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basij \"Basij\") * [State-sponsored foreign militia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Involvement_of_foreign_militias_in_the_suppression_of_protests_in_Iran \"Involvement of foreign militias in the suppression of protests in Iran\") * Iranian counter-protesters[[6]](#cite_note-6)[[7]](#cite_note-7) | | |\n| Lead figures | |\n| *No centralized leadership*[[8]](#cite_note-jpost_blow_up-8)  * [Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") [Ali Khamenei](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Khamenei \"Ali Khamenei\")   ([Supreme Leader of Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Leader_of_Iran \"Supreme Leader of Iran\")) * [Ebrahim Raisi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ebrahim_Raisi \"Ebrahim Raisi\")   ([President of Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Iran \"President of Iran\")) * [Gholam-Hossein Mohseni-Eje'i](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gholam-Hossein_Mohseni-Eje'i \"Gholam-Hossein Mohseni-Eje'i\")   ([Chief Justice of Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chief_Justice_of_Iran \"Chief Justice of Iran\")) * [Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") [Hossein Ashtari](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hossein_Ashtari \"Hossein Ashtari\")   (Chief Commander of the [Police Command of the Islamic Republic of Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Police_Command_of_the_Islamic_Republic_of_Iran \"Police Command of the Islamic Republic of Iran\") * [Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") [Hossein Salami](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hossein_Salami \"Hossein Salami\")   (Commander of the [Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps Ground Forces](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamic_Revolutionary_Guard_Corps_Ground_Forces \"Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps Ground Forces\")) * [Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") [Gholamreza Soleimani](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gholamreza_Soleimani \"Gholamreza Soleimani\")   (Commander of the [Basij](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basij \"Basij\")) | |\n| Casualties | |\n| Deaths | At least 551 protesters including 68 minors killed ([Iran Human Rights](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran_Human_Rights \"Iran Human Rights\")) as of 15 September 2023[[9]](#cite_note-IHR551-9) 200 killed (state media) as of 3 December 2022[[10]](#cite_note-ReutersIrangov-10)  See [casualties](#Casualties) for details. |\n| Arrested | As many as 19,262 ([HRANA](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_Rights_Activists_in_Iran \"Human Rights Activists in Iran\"), as of 6 January 2023).[[11]](#cite_note-Reuters12345-11) See [detainees](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Detainees_of_the_September_2022_Iranian_protests \"Detainees of the September 2022 Iranian protests\") for notable cases. |\n\n[Civil unrest](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_unrest \"Civil unrest\") and protests against the [government of the Islamic Republic of Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Iran \"Government of Iran\") associated with the [death in police custody](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_in_custody \"Death in custody\") of [Mahsa Amini](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_of_Mahsa_Amini#Victim \"Death of Mahsa Amini\") ([Persian](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persian_language \"Persian language\"): مهسا امینی) began on 16 September 2022 and carried on into 2023, but by spring 2023, the protests had largely subsided,[[12]](#cite_note-Baloch-F24-20-3-23-12)[[13]](#cite_note-Motamedi-2023-13) ultimately leaving the political leadership unchanged and firmly entrenched in power.[[14]](#cite_note-Hafezi_12_September_2023-14) The protests were described as \"unlike any the country had seen before\",[[15]](#cite_note-Nimoni-BBC-anniversary-2023-15) the \"biggest challenge\" to the government,[[16]](#cite_note-Guardian6November-16) and \"most widespread revolt\"[[17]](#cite_note-Moaveni-NYer-7-8-2023-17) since the [Islamic Revolution](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_Revolution \"Iranian Revolution\") in 1979.\n\nAmini was arrested by the [Guidance Patrol](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guidance_Patrol \"Guidance Patrol\") on 13 September 2022 for allegedly violating [Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\")'s [mandatory hijab law](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hijab_by_country#Iran \"Hijab by country\") by wearing her hijab \"improperly\" while visiting Tehran from [Saqqez](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saqqez \"Saqqez\"). According to eyewitnesses, she was severely beaten by Guidance Patrol officers (this was denied by Iranian authorities).[[18]](#cite_note-Strzyżyńska-guardian-22-9-2022-18) She subsequently collapsed, was hospitalized and died three days later.[[18]](#cite_note-Strzyżyńska-guardian-22-9-2022-18) As the protests spread from Amini's hometown of Saqqez to other cities in the [Iranian Kurdistan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_Kurdistan \"Iranian Kurdistan\") and throughout Iran, the government responded with widespread [Internet blackouts](#Communications_blackouts), nationwide restrictions on social media usage,[[19]](#cite_note-internetrestr-19)[[20]](#cite_note-20) [tear gas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tear_gas \"Tear gas\") and gunfire.[[21]](#cite_note-IHR20220923-21)[[22]](#cite_note-guar26-22)[[23]](#cite_note-23)\n\nAlthough the protests have not been as deadly as those in [2019](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019%E2%80%932020_Iranian_protests \"2019–2020 Iranian protests\") (when more than 1,500 were killed),[[24]](#cite_note-:1-24) they have been \"nationwide, spread across social classes, universities, the streets [and] schools\".[[16]](#cite_note-Guardian6November-16) At least 551 people, including 68 minors, had been killed as a result of the government's intervention in the protests, as of 15 September 2023.[[note 1]](#cite_note-25) Before February 2023 when most were pardoned,[[13]](#cite_note-Motamedi-2023-13) an estimated 19,262 were arrested[[note 2]](#cite_note-26) across at least 134 cities and towns and 132 universities.[[note 3]](#cite_note-27)[[25]](#cite_note-auto2-28)[[26]](#cite_note-Iran's_Ferocious_Dissent-29)\n\nFemale protesters, including schoolchildren, have played a key role in the demonstrations. In addition to demands for increased rights for women, the protests have demanded the overthrow of the Islamic Republic, setting them apart from previous major protest movements in Iran, which have focused on election results or economic woes.[[27]](#cite_note-30)\nThe government's response to the protests and its \"brutal and disproportionate use of force against peaceful protesters and children\" was widely condemned,[[28]](#cite_note-USIP-4-11-2022-31) but [Supreme Leader of Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Leader_of_Iran \"Supreme Leader of Iran\") [Ali Khamenei](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Khamenei \"Ali Khamenei\") dismissed the unrest as \"riots\" and part of a \"[hybrid war](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hybrid_war \"Hybrid war\")\" against Iran created by foreign enemy states and dissidents abroad.[[29]](#cite_note-Motamedi3-32)[[30]](#cite_note-Guardian-33)[[31]](#cite_note-:2-34)\n\nOn 2 February 2024, the UN Human Rights Council's [Fact-Finding Mission](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Independent_International_Fact-Finding_Mission_on_the_Islamic_Republic_of_Iran \"Indepe\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 10000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
