{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":10000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Iran%E2%80%93Saudi_Arabia_summit"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Iran%E2%80%93Saudi_Arabia_summit:\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\n| 2023 Iran–Saudi Arabia summit | |\n| --- | --- |\n| Host country | [China](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China \"China\") |\n| Date | 6–10 March 2023 |\n| Cities | [Beijing](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijing \"Beijing\") |\n| Participants | * [China](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China \"China\") [Wang Yi](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wang_Yi \"Wang Yi\") * [Saudi Arabia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saudi_Arabia \"Saudi Arabia\") [Musaad bin Mohammed Al Aiban](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musaad_bin_Mohammed_Al_Aiban \"Musaad bin Mohammed Al Aiban\") * [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") [Ali Shamkhani](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Shamkhani \"Ali Shamkhani\") |\n| Key points | |\n\nThe **2023 Iran–Saudi Arabia summit** was a high-level meeting between [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") and [Saudi Arabia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saudi_Arabia \"Saudi Arabia\") held in [Beijing](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijing \"Beijing\") from March 6 to 10, 2023. Under the mediation of [China](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China \"China\"), Saudi Arabia and Iran, which are considered rivals in the [Middle East](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Middle_East \"Middle East\"), agreed to restore bilateral diplomatic relations at the ambassadorial level.\n\nFrom 2021 to 2022, Saudi Arabia and Iran hosted multiple rounds of dialogue in [Iraq](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iraq \"Iraq\") and [Oman](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oman \"Oman\"). In December 2022, Chinese leader [Xi Jinping](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\") visited Saudi Arabia and attended the first China-Arab States Summit and the China-Gulf Arab States Cooperation Council Summit.[[1]](#cite_note-1) During this period, he met with leaders of several Arab countries, including King [Salman of Saudi Arabia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salman_of_Saudi_Arabia \"Salman of Saudi Arabia\"). In February 2023, Iranian President [Ebrahim Raisi](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ebrahim_Raisi \"Ebrahim Raisi\") visited China and expressed his welcome to China's initiative to achieve security and stability in the Middle East and promote dialogue among countries in the [Persian Gulf](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persian_Gulf \"Persian Gulf\") region.[[2]](#cite_note-2) Wang Di, Director of the Department of Asian and African Affairs of the [Ministry of Foreign Affairs](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Foreign_Affairs_(China) \"Ministry of Foreign Affairs (China)\") of China, said in an interview with *[People's Daily](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Daily \"People's Daily\")* that Xi Jinping personally worked with the leaders of the two countries during his state visit to Saudi Arabia in December 2022 and his reception of Iranian President Raisi in February 2023 to support the development of good-neighborly and friendly relations between Saudi Arabia and Iran.[[3]](#cite_note-3)\n\nThe meeting was held from March 6 to 10, 2023 at the initiative of the [government of China](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_China \"Government of China\") and under the chairmanship and coordination of [Wang Yi](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wang_Yi \"Wang Yi\"), the Director of the [Office of the Central Foreign Affairs Commission](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Office_of_the_Central_Foreign_Affairs_Commission \"Office of the Central Foreign Affairs Commission\").[[4]](#cite_note-4) Saudi delegation was led by Minister of State and National Security Advisor [Musaad bin Mohammed Al Aiban](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musaad_bin_Mohammed_Al_Aiban \"Musaad bin Mohammed Al Aiban\"), while the Iranian delegation was led by Secretary of the Supreme National Security Council [Ali Shamkhani](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Shamkhani \"Ali Shamkhani\"). On March 10, Saudi Arabia and Iran reached an agreement to resume bilateral diplomatic relations.[[5]](#cite_note-5) China, Saudi Arabia and Iran jointly signed and issued a joint statement, emphasizing that the three parties will work together to uphold the basic norms of international relations, respect the sovereignty of all countries, not interfere in the internal affairs of other countries, and promote international and regional peace and security.[[6]](#cite_note-6)[[7]](#cite_note-7)[[8]](#cite_note-8)\n\n### International organizations\n\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=2023_Iran%E2%80%93Saudi_Arabia_summit&action=edit&section=5 \"Edit section: International organizations\")]\n\n* ![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Flag_of_the_United_Nations.svg/40px-Flag_of_the_United_Nations.svg.png) [United Nations](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations \"United Nations\"): UN Secretary-General spokesperson [Stephane Dujarric](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stéphane_Dujarric \"Stéphane Dujarric\") welcomed the agreement, stating that \"Good neighborly relations between Iran and Saudi Arabia are essential for the stability of the Gulf region\".[[15]](#cite_note-:0-15)\n\n### Political organizations\n\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=2023_Iran%E2%80%93Saudi_Arabia_summit&action=edit&section=6 \"Edit section: Political organizations\")]\n\n* ![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Flag_of_Hezbollah_%28thumbnail_placeholder%29.svg/40px-Flag_of_Hezbollah_%28thumbnail_placeholder%29.svg.png) [Hezbollah](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hezbollah \"Hezbollah\") called the meeting a \"good development\".[[15]](#cite_note-:0-15)\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Saudi-Iran_joint_statement_signing_%282023%29.jpg/250px-Saudi-Iran_joint_statement_signing_%282023%29.jpg)](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Saudi-Iran_joint_statement_signing_(2023).jpg)\n\nIranian Foreign Minister [Hossein Amir-Abdollahian](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hossein_Amir-Abdollahian \"Hossein Amir-Abdollahian\") and Saudi Foreign Minister [Faisal bin Farhan Al Saud](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faisal_bin_Farhan_Al_Saud \"Faisal bin Farhan Al Saud\") after signing a joint statement on the restoration of diplomatic relations, with Chinese Foreign Minister [Qin Gang](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Gang \"Qin Gang\") in the background, 6 April 2023\n\nOn April 6, 2023, Chinese State Councilor and Foreign Minister [Qin Gang](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Gang \"Qin Gang\"), Saudi Foreign Minister [Faisal bin Farhan Al Saud](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Faisal_bin_Farhan_Al_Saud \"Faisal bin Farhan Al Saud\"), and Iranian Foreign Minister [Hossein Amir-Abdollahian](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hossein_Amir-Abdollahian \"Hossein Amir-Abdollahian\") met in Beijing.[[16]](#cite_note-16) On the same day, the foreign ministers of Saudi Arabia and Iran signed a joint statement, announcing the resumption of diplomatic relations between the two countries. The two sides agreed to reopen diplomatic missions within the agreed time and to take necessary measures to open the embassies of the two countries in Riyadh and Tehran, as well as the consulates general in Jeddah and Mashhad. In addition, Saudi Arabia and Iran will continue to conduct necessary coordination between technical delegations to explore ways to expand cooperation between the two countries, including the resumption of official delegations, private sector visits and flights, and to facilitate the mutual issuance of visas between the two countries.[[17]](#cite_note-17)\n\nOn June 6, 2023, the Iranian Embassy in Saudi Arabia reopened, with Iranian Deputy Foreign Minister Bigdli and Saudi Deputy Foreign Minister Yousef among the officials from both countries in attendance. On June 7, the Iranian Consulate General in Jeddah and the representative office in the Organization of Islamic Cooperation also resumed operations.[[18]](#cite_note-18) On June 17, 2023, Saudi Foreign Minister Faisal visited Tehran, the capital of Iran, and met with Iranian Foreign Minister Abdulrahman and President Raisi. This was the first visit by a Saudi foreign minister to Iran since 2006.[[19]](#cite_note-19) On August 9, 2023, the Saudi embassy in Iran reopened.[[20]](#cite_note-20) On September 6, 2023, Saudi Arabia and Iran exchanged ambassadors.[[21]](#cite_note-21) On September 24, 2023, the Maldives restored diplomatic relations with Iran.\n\n1. [↑](#cite_ref-1) [\"中华人民共和国、沙特阿拉伯王国、伊朗伊斯兰共和国三方联合声明\"](https://web.archive.org/web/20230312021359/https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E4%B8%AD%E5%8D%8E%E4%BA%BA%E6%B0%91%E5%85%B1%E5%92%8C%E5%9B%BD%E3%80%81%E6%B2%99%E7%89%B9%E9%98%BF%E6%8B%89%E4%BC%AF%E7%8E%8B%E5%9B%BD%E3%80%81%E4%BC%8A%E6%9C%97%E4%BC%8A%E6%96%AF%E5%85%B0%E5%85%B1%E5%92%8C%E5%9B%BD%E4%B8%89%E6%96%B9%E8%81%94%E5%90%88%E5%A3%B0%E6%98%8E). Archived from [the original](https://zh.wikisource.org/wiki/%E4%B8%AD%E5%8D%8E%E4%BA%BA%E6%B0%91%E5%85%B1%E5%92%8C%E5%9B%BD%E3%80%81%E6%B2%99%E7%89%B9%E9%98%BF%E6%8B%89%E4%BC%AF%E7%8E%8B%E5%9B%BD%E3%80%81%E4%BC%8A%E6%9C%97%E4%BC%8A%E6%96%AF%E5%85%B0%E5%85%B1%E5%92%8C%E5%9B%BD%E4%B8%89%E6%96%B9%E8%81%94%E5%90%88%E5%A3%B0%E6%98%8E) on 2023-03-12. Retrieved 2023-03-12.\n2. [↑](#cite_ref-2) [\"中华人民共和国和伊朗伊斯兰共和国联合声明（全文）\"](https://web.archive.org/web/20230311033615/http://barcelona.china-consulate.gov.cn/zgyw/202302/t20230216_11025836.htm). 2023-02-16. Archived from [the original](http://barcelona.china-consulate.gov.cn/zgyw/202302/t20230216_11025836.htm) on 2023-03-11. Retrieved 2023-03-11.\n3. [↑](#cite_ref-3) [\"中国外交部官员透露中国促成沙伊复交细节\"](https://web.archive.org/web/20230509111154/https://www.zaobao.com.sg/realtime/china/story20230429-1388816). Archived from [the original](https://www.zaobao.com.sg/realtime/china/story20230429-1388816) on 2023-05-09. Retrieved 2023-05-02.\n4. [↑](#cite_ref-4) 新华社 (2023-03-11). [\"王毅主持沙特和伊朗北京对话闭幕式\"](https://web.archive.org/web/20230313003100/http://www.gov.cn/guowuyuan/2023-03/11/content_5745981.htm). 中国政府网. Archived from [the original](http://www.gov.cn/guowuyuan/2023-03/11/content_5745981.htm) on 2023-03-13. Retrieved 2023-03-12.\n5. [↑](#cite_ref-5) [\"王毅主持沙特和伊朗北京对话闭幕式\"](https://web.archive.org/web/20230313100026/https://www.mfa.gov.cn/zyxw/202303/t20230310_11039120.shtml). 中国外交部. 2023-03-10. Archived from [the original](https://www.mfa.gov.cn/zyxw/202303/t20230310_11039120.shtml) on 2023-03-13. Retrieved 2023-03-11.\n6. [↑](#cite_ref-6)\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 10000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
