s \"Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps\") * [Irregular Warfare Headquarters](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irregular_Warfare_Headquarters \"Irregular Warfare Headquarters\") |\n| Years of service | 1979–1989[[d]](#cite_note-7) |\n| Commands | [Islamic Republic of Iran Armed Forces](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamic_Republic_of_Iran_Armed_Forces \"Islamic Republic of Iran Armed Forces\") |\n| Battles/wars | * [Iranian Revolution](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_Revolution \"Iranian Revolution\") * [Aftermath of the Iranian Revolution](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aftermath_of_the_Iranian_Revolution \"Aftermath of the Iranian Revolution\") ([WIA](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wounded_in_action \"Wounded in action\")) * [Iran–Iraq War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran%E2%80%93Iraq_War \"Iran–Iraq War\")   + [Operation Samen-ol-A'emeh](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operation_Samen-ol-A'emeh \"Operation Samen-ol-A'emeh\")[[4]](#cite_note-raee-8) * [Iran–Israel conflict](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran%E2%80%93Israel_conflict \"Iran–Israel conflict\")   + [2024 Iran–Israel conflict](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_Iran%E2%80%93Israel_conflict \"2024 Iran–Israel conflict\")   + [Twelve-Day War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twelve-Day_War \"Twelve-Day War\")   + [2026 Iran war](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Iran_war \"2026 Iran war\") [**X**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Ali_Khamenei \"Assassination of Ali Khamenei\") |\n|  | |\n| Personal life | |\n| Main interests | * [Uṣūl al-Fiqh](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principles_of_Islamic_jurisprudence \"Principles of Islamic jurisprudence\") * [Tafsir](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tafsir \"Tafsir\")[[5]](#cite_note-cgie-9) |\n| Notable idea | [Fatwa against nuclear weapons](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatwa_against_nuclear_weapons \"Fatwa against nuclear weapons\") |\n| Religious life | |\n| Religion | [Islam](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islam_in_Iran \"Islam in Iran\") |\n| Denomination | [Twelver Shi'a](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twelver_Shi'a \"Twelver Shi'a\") |\n| Jurisprudence | [Ja'fari](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ja'fari \"Ja'fari\") |\n| Creed | [Usuli](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Usuli \"Usuli\") |\n| Muslim leader | |\n| Teacher | * [Husayn Burujardi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Husayn_Burujardi \"Husayn Burujardi\") * Ruhollah Khomeini[[5]](#cite_note-cgie-9) |\n| Khamenei speaking at the Hussainiya of Lovers of Karbala in [Sari, Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sari,_Iran \"Sari, Iran\") Recorded 14 October 1995 | |\n|  | |\n\n**Ali Hosseini Khamenei**[[e]](#cite_note-10) (19 April 1939 – 28 February 2026) was an Iranian politician and [Shia cleric](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shia_cleric \"Shia cleric\") who served as the second [supreme leader of Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_leader_of_Iran \"Supreme leader of Iran\") from 1989 until [his assassination in 2026](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Ali_Khamenei \"Assassination of Ali Khamenei\"). A member of the [Khamenei family](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khamenei_family \"Khamenei family\") who held the title [Grand Ayatollah](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Ayatollah \"Grand Ayatollah\"), he previously served as the third [president of Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Iran \"President of Iran\") from 1981 to 1989. His 36-year tenure as supreme leader made him the longest-serving head of state in West Asia at the time of his death.\n\nBorn in [Mashhad](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mashhad \"Mashhad\") to the [Khamenei family](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khamenei_family \"Khamenei family\"), he studied at a [hawza](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawza \"Hawza\") there before settling in [Qom](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qom \"Qom\") in 1958, where he attended the classes of [Ruhollah Khomeini](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruhollah_Khomeini \"Ruhollah Khomeini\"). Khamenei became involved in opposition to [Mohammad Reza Pahlavi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammad_Reza_Pahlavi \"Mohammad Reza Pahlavi\"), and was arrested six times before being exiled for three years by the [Pahlavi government](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pahlavi_government \"Pahlavi government\"). Khamenei was a mainstream figure in the [Iranian Revolution](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_Revolution \"Iranian Revolution\"), and upon its success, held many posts in the newly established [Islamic republic](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamic_republic \"Islamic rep\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 10000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
