{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":10000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019%E2%80%932020_Iranian_protests"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019%E2%80%932020_Iranian_protests:\n| 2019–2020 Iranian protests | |\n| --- | --- |\n|  | |\n| Date | 15–19 November 2019 (4 days, main phase) Spillover clashes lasted until 16 July 2020 (8 months and 1 day) |\n| Location | Throughout [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\"), in 29 provinces, 104 cities and 719 places.[[1]](#cite_note-1) |\n| Caused by | * Increase in fuel prices * Crackdowns of previous waves of the Iranian Democracy Movement, such as the [2017–2018 Iranian protests](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2017–2018_Iranian_protests \"2017–2018 Iranian protests\"), resulting in failures to deliver the demands of the movement * Escalation of the [2018–2019 Iranian general strikes and protests](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018–2019_Iranian_general_strikes_and_protests \"2018–2019 Iranian general strikes and protests\") occurring as part of the Iranian Democracy Movement * Government corruption * Poverty * Human rights abuses * Opposition to President [Hassan Rouhani](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hassan_Rouhani \"Hassan Rouhani\") and Supreme Leader [Ali Khamenei](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Khamenei \"Ali Khamenei\") * Opposition to the [Islamic Republic](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") * Opposition to Iranian involvement in regional conflicts * Opposition to [Anti-Americanism in Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-Americanism_in_Iran \"Anti-Americanism in Iran\") * The shootdown of [Ukraine International Airlines Flight 752](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ukraine_International_Airlines_Flight_752 \"Ukraine International Airlines Flight 752\") (PS752) by the Iranian Government |\n| Goals | * Social and economic stability * Prosecution of corrupt government officials * Removal of [Ali Khamenei](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Khamenei \"Ali Khamenei\") * Regime change and removal of the Islamic Republic of [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") |\n| Methods | [Demonstrations](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demonstration_(people) \"Demonstration (people)\"), riots, [sit-ins](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sit-in \"Sit-in\"), [civil resistance](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_resistance \"Civil resistance\"), [strikes](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_strike \"General strike\"), [online activisms](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Online_activism \"Online activism\"), arson |\n| Result | * Protests violently crushed by government troops * [Internet blackout imposed by government](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019_Internet_blackout_in_Iran \"2019 Internet blackout in Iran\") * Continued growth and rise of the Iranian Democracy Movement, leading to further protests in the movement such as [2021–2022 Iranian protests](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021–2022_Iranian_protests \"2021–2022 Iranian protests\") and the [Mahsa Amini protests](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahsa_Amini_protests \"Mahsa Amini protests\") |\n| Parties | |\n| |  |  | | --- | --- | | **Protesters:**   * Support by most anti-Islamic Republic organizations * [Pahlavi Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pahlavi_Iran \"Pahlavi Iran\") [Monarchist](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monarchism_in_Iran \"Monarchism in Iran\")   **International support:**   * [Human Rights Watch](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_Rights_Watch \"Human Rights Watch\") (HRW) * [Amnesty International](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amnesty_International \"Amnesty International\") | * [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") [Government of Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Islamic_Republic_of_Iran \"Government of Islamic Republic of Iran\")    Pro-government protesters[[2]](#cite_note-2)[[3]](#cite_note-3) | | |\n| Lead figures | |\n| *No centralized leadership*  [Ali Khamenei](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Khamenei \"Ali Khamenei\")   [Hassan Rouhani](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hassan_Rouhani \"Hassan Rouhani\")  [Ebrahim Raisi](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ebrahim_Raisi \"Ebrahim Raisi\")  [Ali Larijani](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Larijani \"Ali Larijani\")  [Hossein Salami](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hossein_Salami \"Hossein Salami\") [Rahmani Fazli](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abdolreza_Rahmani_Fazli \"Abdolreza Rahmani Fazli\")  [Hossein Ashtari](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hossein_Ashtari \"Hossein Ashtari\")  [Azari Jahromi](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammad-Javad_Azari_Jahromi \"Mohammad-Javad Azari Jahromi\") | |\n| Number | |\n| |  |  | | --- | --- | | c. 200,000[[4]](#cite_note-4)[[5]](#cite_note-5) | 100,000-150,000 | | |\n| Casualties and losses | |\n| |  |  | | --- | --- | | * 225 killed (per Interior Ministry)[[6]](#cite_note-6)[[7]](#cite_note-7) * 305+ protesters and bystanders killed (per [Amnesty International](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amnesty_International \"Amnesty International\") and [HRW](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HRW \"HRW\"))[[8]](#cite_note-8) * 1,500 in total killed (per [Reuters](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reuters \"Reuters\"))[[9]](#cite_note-do_whatever-9) * 1,000+ killed (per [United States Department of State](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/US_State_Department \"US State Department\")[[10]](#cite_note-10) * 7,000+ arrested[[11]](#cite_note-11) | 731 banks and 140 government sites torched (per [Abdolreza Rahmani Fazli](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abdolreza_Rahmani_Fazli \"Abdolreza Rahmani Fazli\"))[[12]](#cite_note-12) | | |\n| Casualties | |\n| Arrested | 7,000+ arrested |\n\nThe **2019–2020 Iranian protests**, sometimes known by the protesters as **Bloody November** or (using the [Iranian calendar](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_calendar \"Iranian calendar\")) **Bloody Aban** ([Persian](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Persian_language \"Persian language\"): آبان خونین), were a series of nationwide civil protests in [Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") that took place in 2019 and 2020. Initially caused by a 50–200% increase in fuel prices,[[13]](#cite_note-13)[[14]](#cite_note-14)[[15]](#cite_note-15) they occurred as part of the wider Iranian Democracy Movement, leading to calls for the overthrow of the [government in Iran](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_the_Islamic_Republic_of_Iran \"Government of the Islamic Republic of Iran\") and [Supreme Leader](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Leader_of_Iran \"Supreme Leader of Iran\") [Ali Khamenei](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Khamenei \"Ali Khamenei\").[[16]](#cite_note-auto1-16)[[17]](#cite_note-:0-17)\nThe protests commenced as peaceful gatherings on the evening of 15 November but spread to 21 cities within hours, as videos of the protest circulated online,[[18]](#cite_note-18)[[19]](#cite_note-veconomist1-19)[[20]](#cite_note-20)[[21]](#cite_note-21)[[22]](#cite_note-nytimes.com-22)\neventually becoming the most violent and severe anti-government unrest since the [Iranian Revolution](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_Revolution \"Iranian Revolution\") in 1979.[[23]](#cite_note-23)[[24]](#cite_note-auto5-24)\n\nTo block the sharing of information regarding the protests and the deaths of hundreds of protesters on social media platforms, the government shut down the Internet nationwide, resulting in a near-total internet blackout of around six days.[[25]](#cite_note-25)[[26]](#cite_note-telegraph.co.uk-26)[[27]](#cite_note-albawaba.com-27)\nIn an effort to crush the protests, the Iranian government (according to [Amnesty International](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amnesty_International \"Amnesty International\")) shot protesters dead from rooftops, helicopters, and at close range with machine gun fire.\nIn an effort to mask the scale and casualty count of the protests, it hauled away large numbers of bodies of the dead protesters,[[24]](#cite_note-auto5-24) and threatened families of slain protesters not to speak to the media or hold funerals.[[28]](#cite_note-28)\n\nAs many as 2,000 Iranian protesters were killed.[[9]](#cite_note-do_whatever-9)[[29]](#cite_note-29)[[30]](#cite_note-30) The government crackdown and protests resulted in the destruction of 731 government banks including Iran's central bank, nine [Islamic](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamic \"Islamic\") religious centres, protesters tearing down [anti-American](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-American \"Anti-American\") billboards, and posters and statues of Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei as well as former leader [Ruhollah Khomeini](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruhollah_Khomeini \"Ruhollah Khomeini\"). Fifty government military bases were also attacked by protesters.[[31]](#cite_note-31)[[32]](#cite_note-32) The Iranian regime also employed a week long [nationwide internet shutdown](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019_Internet_blackout_in_Iran \"2019 Internet blackout in Iran\") becoming the longest total Internet shutdown in a large country.[[33]](#cite_note-:2b-33) It was also the first blackout that effectively isolated a whole nation.[[34]](#cite_note-34)\n\nThe uprising, as well as the wider Iranian Democracy Movement in general, differed from [earlier protests in 2009](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2009_Iranian_presidential_election_protests \"2009 Iranian presidential election protests\") in not being limited to students and large cities, and in the speed, severity and higher death toll of the government crackdown, which crushed the uprising in three days,[[35]](#cite_note-Filkins-iran-5-18-2020-35) although protests flared up periodically in the months after.\n\nThe protests, which have occurred at various stages and times since the mid-2010s, increasing in both support and number each time, have found popular support amongst many Iranians. They have the intention of removing the Iranian government and addressing both economic and social issues within Iran, and are often fueled by low wages, unemployment, inflation, government corruption, an [ongoing water crisis](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_crisis_in_Iran \"Water crisis in Iran\"), disillusion amongst Iranian youth and by their [Burnt Generation](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burnt_Generation \"Burnt Generation\") parents with the government's [Islamist](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Islamism \"Islamism\"), anti-Western outlook, the isolation of Iran internationally, [Iranian nationalist](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iranian_nationalism \"Iranian nationalism\") fervor and the government's handling of the [COVID-19 pandemic](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic \"COVID-19 pandemi\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 10000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
